# Feature 14 — Brand Tone Guidelines Upload

## Goal
Allow designated users to upload HungerStation's brand tone and voice 
guidelines once, stored centrally, and used as context for ALL copy 
generation across the app for every user.

## Context
Currently tone is selected from preset pills (Friendly, Professional, 
etc.). The brand guidelines document gives the AI deeper context about 
HungerStation's actual voice, do's and don'ts, terminology, and style 
so generated copy is more on-brand. This should apply globally, not 
per request.

## Access Control
- Only users with an "admin" capability can upload or update the 
  guidelines
- For now, since there is no admin role yet, allow any Copy Team 
  member to upload/update guidelines (they own brand voice)
- All users (Designers and Copy Team) benefit from the guidelines 
  automatically during generation

## Where It Lives
- Add a new page at /guidelines
- Add a "Guidelines" link in the main navigation (visible to all, 
  but upload controls only shown to Copy Team)

## Guidelines Page UI
- Page title: "Brand Tone Guidelines"
- Subtitle: "These guidelines are used as context for all copy 
  generated in Lahjah."
- If guidelines exist:
  - Show the current guidelines content in a readable format
  - Show who last updated it and when
  - Copy Team sees an "Edit guidelines" button
- If no guidelines exist yet:
  - Show empty state: "No brand guidelines uploaded yet."
  - Copy Team sees an "Add guidelines" button

## Upload / Edit Methods
Support two ways to provide guidelines:

1. PASTE TEXT (primary)
   - A large textarea where Copy Team can paste/write the brand 
     voice and tone guidelines directly
   - Rich enough to hold several paragraphs, do's and don'ts, 
     terminology notes
   - "Save guidelines" button (yellow #FFEA00)

2. UPLOAD DOCUMENT (optional)
   - Allow uploading a PDF or DOCX file with the guidelines
   - Store the file in Firebase Storage
   - Extract the text content from the document so it can be used 
     as AI context
   - For PDF: extract text server-side
   - For DOCX: extract text server-side
   - Show the extracted text in the textarea so it can be reviewed 
     and edited before saving

## Data Structure
Store in Firestore at settings/brandGuidelines:
- content (string — the full guidelines text used as AI context)
- fileUrl (optional — link to uploaded source document)
- fileName (optional — original file name)
- updatedBy (uid)
- updatedByName (displayName)
- updatedAt (timestamp)

## Using Guidelines in Generation
- When generating copy (in /api/generate), fetch the brand guidelines 
  from settings/brandGuidelines
- Prepend the guidelines to the system prompt as context, something like:
  "Follow these HungerStation brand tone and voice guidelines when 
  generating copy: [guidelines content]"
- This applies to BOTH the structured request generation AND the 
  /chat AI assistant
- If no guidelines exist, generation works as before (no breakage)

## Firestore Rules
Make sure settings/{document} allows:
- read: any authenticated user
- write: any authenticated user (for now, since no admin role yet)
This is already covered by the existing settings rule.

